{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNKi3cSpwMPgCy7VZxiu1g","type":"tool_result","content":"../skill/SKILL.md\n\n../skill:\nSKILL.md\nheuristics\nprescan\nreferences\nscripts\n\n../skill/heuristics:\nagent.yaml\nbuild-time.yaml\nconfiguration.yaml\necosystem.yaml\nrun-time.yaml\n\n../skill/prescan:\npatterns.yaml\n\n../skill/references:\nagent.md\nbuild-time.md\nchecks.json\nconfiguration.md\necosystem.md\nrun-time.md\n\n../skill/scripts:\n__pycache__\nanswer.py\nchallenge.py\nmerge_findings.py\nnew_findings.py\nprescan.py\ntest_challenge.py\ntest_prescan.py\nvalidate_findings.py\n{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"agent (clinic-agent, Northbay Clinic Group scheduling agent; local copy, no git)\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T16:07:59Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Reviewed all 36 files under agent/: src (loop, executor, registry, metadata scan, approvals, budget, kill switch, identity, audit, classifier, integrations, routes, reminders worker), config, prompts, release manifest, Dockerfile, k8s manifests, Terraform, CI/deploy workflows, CODEOWNERS and tests. Not found: .brace/ record, package-lock.json, MCP gateway, admission policy, SIEM/alert routing, drift tooling, rollback runbook, staff console and approval service, EHR/payments/SMS/eligibility server code, chat widget. Nothing was run; code read only. Reviewer model: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5). Step 8 challenges have NOT been run: all likely_pass items and the R04 N/A candidate are unchallenged. Normal mode, no --conservative. All 11 pre-scan hits resolved (H001-H008 and H005 dismissed, H009/H010 confirmed under R13, H011 confirmed under E03).\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A01\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Distinct agent identity\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Give the agent its own non-human identity. Keep it separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Show that permissions and revocation belong to that identity, even when a user starts the run.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Instance or tenant labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A credential scoped to more operations, resources, or tenants than needed\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens not measured\",\n          \"owner\": \"B04\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"likely_pass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 60,\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account bound to the clinic-agent-runtime IRSA role; only the agent's own reminder CronJob shares the role (deployment.yaml:27)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The agent runs under its own workload principal (service account, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID) that no other service or unrelated agent uses.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the agent's identity: pod `serviceAccountName`, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID in IaC or deploy config. 2) Search other deployments, services, and agents in the repo for the same name or role. 3) Answer no if it is shared, `default`, the main backend's identity, or only a string label with no credential. Answer unknown if identity is assigned outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:60\",\n          \"quote\": \"serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched other deployments, services and roles in the repo for the same account or role: none belong to unrelated services.\",\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account bound to the clinic-agent-runtime IRSA role; only the agent's own reminder CronJob shares the role (deployment.yaml:27)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Tool and API clients get credentials from the agent's own principal, not from the launching user's forwarded token or session cookie.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find every place tool and API clients get a token or key. 2) Trace where each comes from: workload identity or token exchange, versus the incoming request's `Authorization` header or session cookie. 3) Check every client, not just the main one. 4) Answer no if any client forwards the user's token or cookie as-is, or uses a shared static key.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:56\",\n          \"quote\": \"const token = await exchangeToken(opts.workloadToken, req.clinicId, req.patientId);\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for forwarding of the chat JWT or Authorization header into tool clients: webchat.ts only verifies the JWT; no client receives it.\",\n          \"note\": \"Peer calls use a token exchanged from the workload token; EHR, payments and SMS use per-clinic service credentials from Secrets Manager\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.3\",\n          \"check\": \"When a user starts a run, the user is carried as a delegated subject (for example a token exchange with separate act and sub), while the agent keeps its own principal.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the code that starts a run for a user. 2) Look for token exchange (RFC 8693, `subject_token`, `actor_token`, `act`/`sub` claims) or a separate delegated-subject field. 3) Check the agent's own principal is still the actor. 4) Answer no if the user's token is used directly or the user replaces the agent identity. Answer unknown if the exchange happens in an outside identity service.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/identity.ts:70\",\n          \"quote\": \"subject: Subject;\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for code that replaces agent identity with the user: none; audit records keep subject and agent fields apart (recorder.ts:35).\",\n          \"note\": \"RunContext carries the patient or staff user as a separate subject while the agent's own identity() fields are unchanged\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Permissions are bound to the agent principal in IaC or RBAC, so revoking that principal alone removes the agent's access without disabling the user.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find IAM policies, RoleBindings, or grants in Terraform, Helm, or Kubernetes YAML. 2) Check they bind to the agent principal, not to a user, group, or shared role. 3) Check that removing that binding alone would cut the agent's access. 4) Answer no if access depends on the user's grants or a shared credential. Answer unknown if permissions are not defined in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:3\",\n          \"quote\": \"resource \\\"aws_iam_role\\\" \\\"runtime\\\" {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for grants to users or groups on agent resources: only the ops kill-switch role (iam.tf:60-86).\",\n          \"note\": \"Secrets, DynamoDB and Firehose grants are bound to the agent's own role; deleting it removes agent access without touching users (breadth is filed under B02)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Agent has its own service account and IAM role and carries the user as a separate subject.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Run the A01 recipe: revoke the agent role alone.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\",\n      \"challenge\": {\n        \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n        \"note\": \"I found no failing control; the only soft spot is that the eligibility token exchange does not carry the user as a cryptographic actor/subject pair.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A02\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"All six identity fields\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Check that every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context. Look at successful, denied, failed, and background actions, not just the main request path.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Identity labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent-type-id not computed as a hash of its identity inputs\",\n          \"owner\": \"A03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent able to erase or rewrite its own audit history\",\n          \"owner\": \"E10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Sub-agent record missing its parent link or parent prompt\",\n          \"owner\": \"A06\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts\",\n          \"line\": 9,\n          \"note\": \"IdentityFields has accountableParty, operationalOwner, tenantId, agentTypeId, agentInstanceId and traceparent, all required (recorder.ts:8-15)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The audit record schema has all six fields: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the audit record schema or the function that writes audit entries. 2) Check for each of the six: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, `agent.type.id`, `agent.instance.id`, trace context (`traceparent` or trace and span IDs). 3) Answer no if any one is missing from the schema or never set.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts:9\",\n          \"quote\": \"accountableParty: z.string().min(1),\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for audit writers that bypass the schema: audit.record parses every event with AuditEvent (recorder.ts:60).\",\n          \"note\": \"IdentityFields has accountableParty, operationalOwner, tenantId, agentTypeId, agentInstanceId and traceparent, all required (recorder.ts:8-15)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.2\",\n          \"check\": \"All six fields are written on denied, failed, async, and background actions too, not only on the successful main request path.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) List every path that writes an audit record, or should: success, policy deny, `except`/`catch` blocks, retries, queue workers, cron jobs, webhooks, other endpoints such as approvals, and refusals before the run starts (quota, rate limit, auth) that return an error without logging. 2) For each, check all six fields are set, ideally by one shared wrapper. 3) Answer no if any deny, error, async, or background path writes records without them, or writes no record at all.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:57\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (!parsed.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \\\"invalid payload\\\" });\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Requests refused before a run starts (invalid SMS payload, unknown number, failed web chat auth at webchat.ts:24,36 and unknown clinic at webchat.ts:45) return errors with no audit record. Inside runs, deny, failed and background paths carry all six fields.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Trace context (trace and span IDs) is stored in the audit record itself, not only in separate tracing spans.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check it stores trace and span IDs (or `traceparent`) as fields in the record itself. 3) Answer no if trace context exists only in OpenTelemetry spans, or the record's trace field is never filled.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n  305690 brace-findings.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07bbb101-4eaa-4940-9778-fd11038ec616","uuid":"14b6621d-71a9-4b66-a0fa-c57b41a51fa9","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:30:32.818Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"../skill/SKILL.md\n\n../skill:\nSKILL.md\nheuristics\nprescan\nreferences\nscripts\n\n../skill/heuristics:\nagent.yaml\nbuild-time.yaml\nconfiguration.yaml\necosystem.yaml\nrun-time.yaml\n\n../skill/prescan:\npatterns.yaml\n\n../skill/references:\nagent.md\nbuild-time.md\nchecks.json\nconfiguration.md\necosystem.md\nrun-time.md\n\n../skill/scripts:\n__pycache__\nanswer.py\nchallenge.py\nmerge_findings.py\nnew_findings.py\nprescan.py\ntest_challenge.py\ntest_prescan.py\nvalidate_findings.py\n{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"agent (clinic-agent, Northbay Clinic Group scheduling agent; local copy, no git)\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T16:07:59Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Reviewed all 36 files under agent/: src (loop, executor, registry, metadata scan, approvals, budget, kill switch, identity, audit, classifier, integrations, routes, reminders worker), config, prompts, release manifest, Dockerfile, k8s manifests, Terraform, CI/deploy workflows, CODEOWNERS and tests. Not found: .brace/ record, package-lock.json, MCP gateway, admission policy, SIEM/alert routing, drift tooling, rollback runbook, staff console and approval service, EHR/payments/SMS/eligibility server code, chat widget. Nothing was run; code read only. Reviewer model: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5). Step 8 challenges have NOT been run: all likely_pass items and the R04 N/A candidate are unchallenged. Normal mode, no --conservative. All 11 pre-scan hits resolved (H001-H008 and H005 dismissed, H009/H010 confirmed under R13, H011 confirmed unde