{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9AgbtK52TeSjA83DYgYbX","type":"tool_result","content":"item \"C04\"\ngate \"G2\"\ntitle \"Detect drift per agent\"\nrequirement \"Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline. Simulate a prompt edit, an added tool, and a looser egress rule. Check that each one raises an alert and gets the documented response \\u2014 block, quarantine, or rollback \\u2014 within a set time.\"\nnot_covered [\n {\n  \"problem\": \"Hosted model changing behind a fixed name\",\n  \"owner\": \"C05\"\n },\n {\n  \"problem\": \"A tool server changing its description or schema after approval\",\n  \"owner\": \"E03\"\n },\n {\n  \"problem\": \"Who may change production config, and emergency change records\",\n  \"owner\": \"C02\"\n },\n {\n  \"problem\": \"Manifest missing components that define the release\",\n  \"owner\": \"C01\"\n }\n]\nrating \"gap\"\nconfidence \"low\"\nevidence []\nred_flags_found [\n \"src/server.ts:32 The only comparison is a one-time start-up id check by the agent about itself. It covers image digest, harness version/sha and config files. No drift job compares running network policies, MCP server lists, permissions or self-hosted weights against the approved baseline, and none compares the live cluster state at all.\",\n \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:6 No scheduled, admission-webhook or change-event drift check exists. The only trigger is a manual deploy workflow. The only CronJob is the reminders job, which does no drift detection.\",\n \"src/server.ts:34 A mismatch only logs an error and increments a metric, then start-up continues with setAgentTypeId(typeId). There is no block, quarantine or rollback, no response configured, and no time limit.\"\n]\nviolates [\n \"Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline\",\n \"gets the documented response \\u2014 block, quarantine, or rollback \\u2014 within a set time\"\n]\nalso_affects []\nsummary \"No drift detection or response is defined in this repo.\"\nnext_step \"Provide drift tooling, schedule, alert and response time target.\"\nlead_role \"operations\"\nchallenge {\n \"verdict\": \"failed\",\n \"note\": \"Drift detection is limited to a start-up identity check that only logs on mismatch; there is no scheduled drift check, no coverage of network policies, permissions, MCP lists or weights, and no enforced response or time limit.\"\n}\n{\n \"id\": \"C04.1\",\n \"check\": \"A drift check compares running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against the approved baseline, with each of these covered.\",\n \"verify\": \"1) Find the drift check job or tool. 2) List what it compares: images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, self-hosted weights. 3) Check each is compared with the approved baseline, not with the live state itself. 4) Answer no if any category is missing or excluded. Answer unknown if drift detection runs in an outside platform.\",\n \"met\": \"no\",\n \"evidence\": \"src/server.ts:32\",\n \"quote\": \"if (typeId !== manifest.agentTypeId) {\",\n \"counter_search\": \"\",\n \"note\": \"[challenge] The only comparison is a one-time start-up id check by the agent about itself. It covers image digest, harness version/sha and config files. No drift job compares running network policies, MCP server lists, permissions or self-hosted weights against the approved baseline, and none compares the live cluster state at all.\"\n}\n{\n \"id\": \"C04.2\",\n \"check\": \"The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events.\",\n \"verify\": \"1) Find what triggers the drift check: cron or CI schedule, admission webhook, or change events. 2)